WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.596
- We're backstage at HARD Summer.

00:00:02.596 --> 00:00:05.307
Slushii's playing right
now and killing it.

00:00:05.307 --> 00:00:06.957
I imagine he's working up an appetite,

00:00:06.957 --> 00:00:09.117
I'm hungry, I haven't eaten all day.

00:00:09.117 --> 00:00:12.477
The minute he finishes, we're
hopping in a car together,

00:00:12.477 --> 00:00:14.397
and we are gonna search the city

00:00:14.397 --> 00:00:16.808
for the best late-night pizza.

00:00:16.808 --> 00:00:20.373
("Level Up" by Slushii plays)

00:00:20.373 --> 00:00:21.870
- [Cyrus] It's surprisingly
difficult to find

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:24.682
delicious late-night food in Los Angeles.

00:00:24.682 --> 00:00:26.341
Tonight, I'm meeting up
with a fellow night owl

00:00:26.341 --> 00:00:28.351
to explore a restaurant that many say

00:00:28.351 --> 00:00:30.768
is an exception to this rule.

00:00:32.402 --> 00:00:33.235
Are you tired?

00:00:33.235 --> 00:00:34.652
- I am... hungry.

00:00:34.973 --> 00:00:37.082
I'm, like, so ready for pizza right now.

00:00:37.082 --> 00:00:38.522
- You grew up on the East Coast,

00:00:38.522 --> 00:00:40.221
how would you compare
pizza on the East Coast

00:00:40.221 --> 00:00:41.990
to pizza on the West Coast so far?

00:00:41.990 --> 00:00:44.282
- I believe that the
water tastes different.

00:00:44.282 --> 00:00:46.391
Pizza here is so clean-cut that it's like,

00:00:46.391 --> 00:00:48.308
almost, it's like too--

00:00:48.349 --> 00:00:49.182
- It's like boring.

00:00:49.182 --> 00:00:51.522
- I'm not gonna lie, it's weak.

00:00:51.522 --> 00:00:53.230
- I am optimistic about tonight, though.

00:00:53.230 --> 00:00:55.101
We are going to a place
called D'Amore's Pizza.

00:00:55.101 --> 00:00:56.821
It is open 'til four in the morning.

00:00:56.821 --> 00:00:58.271
It's the most late-night pizza in L.A.

00:00:58.271 --> 00:00:59.438
- Let's do it.

00:00:59.586 --> 00:01:00.419
(electronic music)

00:01:00.419 --> 00:01:02.844
- Hey, I'm Joe D'Amore,
founder of D'Amore's Pizza.

00:01:02.844 --> 00:01:05.039
We've been here for 31 years.

00:01:05.039 --> 00:01:06.226
The dough is made in the morning.

00:01:06.226 --> 00:01:09.350
It's rolled into little balls
and put in plastic bags.

00:01:09.350 --> 00:01:13.321
And we unbag it as we use it,
so every pizza is made fresh.

00:01:13.321 --> 00:01:16.572
Except for the slice pies,
they're eighty percent cooked,

00:01:16.572 --> 00:01:18.322
then put in the rack.

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:22.091
And then when someone orders
it, we continue cooking it

00:01:22.091 --> 00:01:25.382
the other twenty percent
as opposed to reheating it.

00:01:25.382 --> 00:01:26.815
It's like a fresh pie.

00:01:26.815 --> 00:01:28.587
(chimes)

00:01:28.587 --> 00:01:30.013
- We grew up on the East
Coast, and we've had trouble

00:01:30.013 --> 00:01:31.854
finding great pizza on the West Coast.

00:01:31.854 --> 00:01:33.485
Why do you think that is?

00:01:33.485 --> 00:01:35.437
- The fact's is the water.

00:01:35.437 --> 00:01:36.800
(Cyrus laughing)
- That's what I said.

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:38.050
- He called it.

00:01:38.149 --> 00:01:40.201
- The water has to be
from Maine to New Jersey,

00:01:40.201 --> 00:01:42.059
as far west as Chicago.

00:01:42.059 --> 00:01:44.959
If you go south of New
Jersey or west of Chicago,

00:01:44.959 --> 00:01:47.241
you rapidly lose the
minerals that are conducive

00:01:47.241 --> 00:01:50.190
to making any kind of
bread dough, bagel dough,

00:01:50.190 --> 00:01:51.931
you talk about the New York bagels.

00:01:51.931 --> 00:01:54.848
For the first 25 years in business,

00:01:55.030 --> 00:01:57.179
I brought the water from Boston.

00:01:57.179 --> 00:01:58.830
I couldn't keep bringing
the water from Boston

00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:00.449
and the flour from Italy,

00:02:00.449 --> 00:02:03.771
so I filled the rest of the
container with Italian water.

00:02:03.771 --> 00:02:06.309
And now I also bring the
tomatoes and the olive oil.

00:02:06.309 --> 00:02:08.990
It makes the flavor, even, so much better.

00:02:08.990 --> 00:02:12.720
- Tell us why you decided
that this restaurant

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:14.054
is open 'til four in the morning.

00:02:14.054 --> 00:02:16.612
- When the bar's close,
they come out at two o'clock

00:02:16.612 --> 00:02:17.516
looking for food.

00:02:17.516 --> 00:02:19.716
So we figured, okay, we'll stay 'til 2:30.

00:02:19.716 --> 00:02:22.386
We stayed 'til 2:30, but
then all of a sudden,

00:02:22.386 --> 00:02:24.196
waitresses and waiters are coming in.

00:02:24.196 --> 00:02:26.241
They have to clean up before they leave.

00:02:26.241 --> 00:02:28.511
Then all of a sudden, we
get all these deliveries.

00:02:28.511 --> 00:02:31.642
Who the heck wants pizza at
3:30, four in the morning?

00:02:31.642 --> 00:02:32.475
I found out.

00:02:32.475 --> 00:02:33.308
(Cyrus laughing)

00:02:33.308 --> 00:02:34.141
I found out.

00:02:34.141 --> 00:02:35.540
Hence, now 10 years later, we're open

00:02:35.540 --> 00:02:37.140
'til four in the morning every night.

00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:38.832
- We're in the market
for three slices tonight.

00:02:38.832 --> 00:02:39.665
What would your--

00:02:39.665 --> 00:02:40.627
- Our most popular?

00:02:40.627 --> 00:02:43.251
- Yeah, what would be the
three recommendations from you?

00:02:43.251 --> 00:02:45.142
- Well you know, still the cheese pizza

00:02:45.142 --> 00:02:47.643
is the most popular pizza in the world.

00:02:47.643 --> 00:02:51.876
Our most popular pizza that
has meat on it is our combo.

00:02:51.876 --> 00:02:55.255
But our most popular pizza
is called the Pizza Bianco.

00:02:55.255 --> 00:02:59.934
It's fresh spinach and roasted
peppers, sauteed in olive oil

00:02:59.934 --> 00:03:02.265
and fresh garlic, topped
with Parmesan, mozzarella,

00:03:02.265 --> 00:03:03.604
and ricotta cheese.

00:03:03.604 --> 00:03:07.505
- Well, we are looking
forward to trying all this.

00:03:07.505 --> 00:03:09.144
Two slices.
- Oh, man.

00:03:09.144 --> 00:03:10.422
(Cyrus laughing)
- Alright, we are in business.

00:03:10.422 --> 00:03:11.255
- Super cool.

00:03:11.255 --> 00:03:12.142
- [Waiter] You guys want
any pepper and Parmesan?

00:03:12.142 --> 00:03:13.225
- Sure.
- Yes.

00:03:13.805 --> 00:03:14.638
- Let's do this.

00:03:14.638 --> 00:03:15.471
- Oh, yeah.

00:03:15.471 --> 00:03:16.435
- So we're starting cheese.

00:03:16.435 --> 00:03:17.352
- It's hot.

00:03:19.577 --> 00:03:20.533
- Oh my goodness.

00:03:20.533 --> 00:03:21.366
- This is East Coast pizza, right?

00:03:21.366 --> 00:03:22.204
- It's East Coast pizza.

00:03:22.204 --> 00:03:23.037
- This is awesome.

00:03:23.037 --> 00:03:26.593
- The crust is just
like, a perfect texture.

00:03:26.593 --> 00:03:27.426
- It's so crunchy.

00:03:27.426 --> 00:03:28.884
- But it still has that, like,

00:03:28.884 --> 00:03:30.345
danger that you're talking
about that you like.

00:03:30.345 --> 00:03:31.642
- This is a perfect balance.

00:03:31.642 --> 00:03:32.815
- Yeah, it's fantastic.

00:03:32.815 --> 00:03:34.015
- It tastes like boardwalk pizza.

00:03:34.015 --> 00:03:35.335
Like, pizza that you get down the Shore.

00:03:35.335 --> 00:03:36.168
- Yeah.

00:03:36.265 --> 00:03:37.444
- On a nice weekend.

00:03:37.444 --> 00:03:39.402
- Do you write music while
you're touring as well,

00:03:39.402 --> 00:03:40.244
on the road?

00:03:40.244 --> 00:03:42.193
- Mhm, especially when,
like, we have runs like this,

00:03:42.193 --> 00:03:44.055
we're just out for days at a time.

00:03:44.055 --> 00:03:46.532
I have a lot of time to,
like, simmer out a few tracks.

00:03:46.532 --> 00:03:49.638
- [Producer] Ever put in
anything weird on your pizza?

00:03:49.638 --> 00:03:52.336
- Yeah. I went on a date
with a girl in Japan.

00:03:52.336 --> 00:03:53.305
She takes me to this place

00:03:53.305 --> 00:03:55.408
where they put maple syrup on pizza.

00:03:55.408 --> 00:03:56.241
- Okay.

00:03:56.241 --> 00:03:57.324
- And it's...

00:03:57.488 --> 00:03:58.321
- Really?

00:03:58.604 --> 00:03:59.854
- It's amazing.

00:04:00.005 --> 00:04:01.505
Ah, this is solid.

00:04:03.681 --> 00:04:05.114
- That is lights out good.

00:04:05.114 --> 00:04:07.408
There's just so much flavor
going on with these toppings.

00:04:07.408 --> 00:04:08.325
- So fresh.

00:04:08.749 --> 00:04:10.728
- Great balance of like,
softness and crispiness.

00:04:10.728 --> 00:04:11.561
- Wow.

00:04:11.869 --> 00:04:13.650
- So, I've got a question
for you. You're 21?

00:04:13.650 --> 00:04:14.483
- Yeah.

00:04:14.483 --> 00:04:15.589
- And can you kind of walk us through

00:04:15.589 --> 00:04:17.099
how Slushii came to be?

00:04:17.099 --> 00:04:19.358
- So, I've been producing
music for, like, a while

00:04:19.358 --> 00:04:21.574
and my Soundcloud got deleted.

00:04:21.574 --> 00:04:23.904
All the copyright strikes
hit at the same time.

00:04:23.904 --> 00:04:26.103
There was no getting it
back and I was just like,

00:04:26.103 --> 00:04:27.093
"Dude, this is it."

00:04:27.093 --> 00:04:29.394
That was like, my livelihood,
quote-unquote, you know?

00:04:29.394 --> 00:04:31.434
I built that over like, three, four years.

00:04:31.434 --> 00:04:33.725
I made the Slushii logo in like a night.

00:04:33.725 --> 00:04:35.622
It was just like a last stitch effort,

00:04:35.622 --> 00:04:36.685
might as well do it right.

00:04:36.685 --> 00:04:38.982
Restart with all the knowledge I have now,

00:04:38.982 --> 00:04:41.065
just kind of went for it.

00:04:43.313 --> 00:04:44.693
- This, this looks amazing.

00:04:44.693 --> 00:04:45.702
- Don't need extra cheese with this one.

00:04:45.702 --> 00:04:46.535
- No, no.

00:04:46.719 --> 00:04:48.645
(crunching)

00:04:48.645 --> 00:04:49.502
- Oh my god.

00:04:49.502 --> 00:04:51.093
- That's game over right there.

00:04:51.093 --> 00:04:52.634
- Let's take it back.

00:04:52.634 --> 00:04:55.453
An important part of your story is

00:04:55.453 --> 00:04:57.493
the life you used to have
and the life you have now.

00:04:57.493 --> 00:04:58.326
- Yeah.

00:04:58.326 --> 00:04:59.586
- Tell us a little about your past

00:04:59.586 --> 00:05:01.515
and what you were going through,

00:05:01.515 --> 00:05:04.182
and how your outlook helped you.

00:05:05.464 --> 00:05:09.115
- So, I wasn't necessarily the
most popular guy in school.

00:05:09.115 --> 00:05:11.314
Didn't really talk to anybody.

00:05:11.314 --> 00:05:12.797
I have Asperger's.

00:05:12.797 --> 00:05:16.856
I was a lot slower socially in
the beginning of high school.

00:05:16.856 --> 00:05:18.957
As a result of that, I would
kind of isolate myself.

00:05:18.957 --> 00:05:21.605
And one thing that really
helped me was music.

00:05:21.605 --> 00:05:23.997
So like, listening to
music, writing songs.

00:05:23.997 --> 00:05:26.525
Once I actually started
to write more and more,

00:05:26.525 --> 00:05:28.828
I kind of realized, I
shouldn't really care

00:05:28.828 --> 00:05:31.214
what people think about, you know, me.

00:05:31.214 --> 00:05:34.881
That really set things
off for who I am now.

00:05:35.070 --> 00:05:38.957
I really don't care what
anybody thinks, you know.

00:05:38.957 --> 00:05:40.290
Look at my hair.

00:05:40.313 --> 00:05:41.993
(Cyrus laughing)
You know, I don't care.

00:05:41.993 --> 00:05:46.011
If there was one clear goal
from the entire Slushii project,

00:05:46.011 --> 00:05:47.923
is it just doesn't matter
where you come from,

00:05:47.923 --> 00:05:49.673
what you look like, what you sound like,

00:05:49.673 --> 00:05:53.523
as long as you have a dream
and you keep driving that home,

00:05:53.523 --> 00:05:55.963
then you can do it, it's possible.

00:05:55.963 --> 00:05:57.093
I'm proof of that.

00:05:57.093 --> 00:06:00.343
I'm just a blue-haired guy from Jersey.

00:06:01.464 --> 00:06:02.352
- We're three slices deep.

00:06:02.352 --> 00:06:05.101
Which, to you, has been
your favorite slice?

00:06:05.101 --> 00:06:06.482
- Uh, the combo, for sure.

00:06:06.482 --> 00:06:08.310
- I'm in the combo vote too.

00:06:08.310 --> 00:06:10.562
- I'm not even like an olive fan at all,

00:06:10.562 --> 00:06:12.733
or mushrooms, and like, just
the way it was put together.

00:06:12.733 --> 00:06:14.581
- It all blends together seamlessly.

00:06:14.581 --> 00:06:17.575
You don't feel gross
after eating it either.

00:06:17.575 --> 00:06:19.179
Would you come back here?

00:06:19.179 --> 00:06:20.854
- This is my new spot.
- This is your new spot?

00:06:20.854 --> 00:06:21.937
- Like, forever.

00:06:21.937 --> 00:06:23.344
- Well, we appreciate you sharing the day

00:06:23.344 --> 00:06:24.375
and the night with us.

00:06:24.375 --> 00:06:25.703
And hopefully, we'll see each other again.

00:06:25.703 --> 00:06:26.965
I'll be over here.

00:06:26.965 --> 00:06:28.634
- Let's grab some pizza some time.

00:06:28.634 --> 00:06:29.695
Thanks for having me.

00:06:29.695 --> 00:06:31.605
- Yeah, thank you so much.

00:06:31.605 --> 00:06:35.535
My tour bus is not here
but I will hail an Uber,

00:06:35.535 --> 00:06:38.354
or perhaps try to find
one of those scooters.

00:06:38.354 --> 00:06:40.854
(dance music)

